The new failure reveals the other API 67.0 change: in Apex queries compiled at API 67.0, fields the running user cannot read are treated as nonexistent columns at query time, so the hard-coded `Internal_Notes__c` in `myOpenTickets()` now throws `QueryException: No such column` for agents — breaking the documented "never fails because of field-level security" behaviour. The fix is to build the field list dynamically from describe results (only readable fields are queried) and keep `Security.stripInaccessible` as the enforcement/stripping mechanism. `searchNotes()` is fixed the same way, still throwing `QueryException` when a queried field is unreadable, as documented. `escalate()` only selects `Id` (always readable) and `openTicketCount()` uses `COUNT()`, so both are unaffected.

