What changed and why:

- LWC template expressions (LWC1060) don't allow `UnaryExpression`, so `hidden={!isExpanded}` is rejected by the compiler, just as the earlier ternary was.
- The negation now lives in the component class: a simple reactive getter `isCollapsed` returns `!this.isExpanded`, and the template binds `hidden={isCollapsed}`.
- Runtime behavior is unchanged and correct: when collapsed, `isCollapsed` is `true` so the `hidden` attribute is present on the `section-body` div; when expanded, LWC removes the boolean `hidden` attribute. The body div stays in the DOM either way, so `aria-controls` always resolves.

